From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob <24017069+wignerStan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:15:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(codex): forward native response.interrupt on duplex sessions

Forward the original interrupt control on the existing authenticated duplex
socket. Reuse the steering control writer, credential check and request capture.
Keep upstream acknowledgements, incomplete boundaries and client continuation
under upstream/client control without creating steering successor state.

Test the native executor and actual Gin/auth/executor route with an active
response, exact interrupt bytes, upstream interrupt events, terminal usage and
explicit continuation on one connection. Reject controls after credential
revocation. Existing response-steering configuration and defaults are unchanged.

---
